---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { datasetJsonLd } from '../../lib/seo';

const pricing = await getCollection('pricing');

/* Structural metrics per provider: tier spread, output/input ratio, cache depth.
   Derived from the same records the table renders, never hand-written. */
const structure = pricing.map((p) => {
  const inputs = p.data.models.map((m) => m.input_price_per_1m).filter((x): x is number => x != null);
  const ratios = p.data.models
    .filter((m) => m.input_price_per_1m && m.output_price_per_1m)
    .map((m) => m.output_price_per_1m! / m.input_price_per_1m!);
  const caches = p.data.models
    .filter((m) => m.input_price_per_1m && m.cached_input_price_per_1m)
    .map((m) => (m.cached_input_price_per_1m! / m.input_price_per_1m!) * 100);
  return {
    id: p.id,
    currency: p.data.currency,
    models: p.data.models.length,
    minInput: Math.min(...inputs),
    maxInput: Math.max(...inputs),
    spread: Math.max(...inputs) / Math.min(...inputs),
    ratio: ratios.length ? ratios.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / ratios.length : null,
    cache: caches.length ? Math.min(...caches) : null,
  };
});
const pricingPageUrl = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).href;
const pricingDataset = datasetJsonLd({
  id: pricingPageUrl,
  name: 'China AI API Pricing Database',
  description: 'Time-stamped Chinese AI API pricing snapshots: input, output, cached and batch prices per 1M tokens with sources and effective dates.',
  dateModified: pricing.map((x) => x.data.last_verified).sort().at(-1),
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chinese AI API Pricing: Every Model, Normalised"
  description="Normalised API pricing for Chinese models in USD per 1M tokens: input, output, cached and batch rates, with currency, region and effective dates."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Chinese AI API Pricing</h1>
  <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6 max-w-2xl">
    Prices normalized to USD per 1 million tokens, with currency, region, billing mode, effective dates and
    official sources preserved. Pricing is time-sensitive — always check the verification date.
  </p>

    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(pricingDataset)} />

  <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 mb-8 text-gray-800">
    <p><strong>Short answer.</strong> Chinese API list prices have converged on a shape: input around $0.15 for a flash tier, output at 3–5x input, and a cache hit at 2–20% of input. What differs — and what actually decides your bill — is the structure around the price: time-of-day tiers, context cliffs, cache residency charges, batch availability and the currency you are invoiced in.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold pt-2">The $0.15 floor is real, and it is not the whole story</h2>
    <p>Six providers, and almost every one has a model at or near $0.15 per 1M input tokens. That number has become the market's anchor, and it is genuinely available — Qwen3.8-Flash, GLM-5.3-Flash and DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash all sit there. But the floor is a floor on <em>input</em>, and input is rarely the dominant cost.</p>
    <p>Output is where bills are made. At a 4:1 ratio — the median here — a workload that generates 500 tokens for every 100 it reads spends 95% of its money on output. Comparing two models at the same input price but different output ratios is comparing the smaller half of the bill.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold pt-2">Cache depth varies by a factor of ten</h2>
    <p>The cache discount is the second lever, and it is the one buyers under-use. A cache hit costs 2% of input at DeepSeek, 10–12% at Moonshot and Alibaba, and 20% at ByteDance, MiniMax and Zhipu. On an agent loop that re-reads a 40K-token system prompt twenty times, that difference is larger than the gap between the headline prices.</p>
    <p>The catch is that caching rewards stable prefixes. Prompts that reshuffle context on every call — the common RAG pattern — get little benefit from any provider, and should be optimised before the provider is chosen.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold pt-2">Structure beats list price</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Time-of-day pricing</strong> (DeepSeek): the cheap rate is available to queues, not to chat. A European product's working day overlaps the peak window.</li>
      <li><strong>Context cliffs</strong> (MiniMax): above 512K input tokens the whole call doubles, so a 1M-context model is not flat-priced across its window.</li>
      <li><strong>Tier spreads</strong> (Zhipu 9x, Moonshot 20x): the same family sold at wildly different prices, which makes routing — not provider choice — the biggest cost lever.</li>
      <li><strong>Cache residency</strong> (ByteDance): the only provider charging for cache storage per hour, which punishes caches that are created and forgotten.</li>
      <li><strong>Currency</strong> (ByteDance, CNY only): the dollar cost is an FX decision, and the invoice may not fit your finance system.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold pt-2">Read the table below with three questions</h2>
    <p>First, what does a completed task cost at your output length — not at your input length. Second, what fraction of your prompt is a stable prefix that can be cached. Third, which tier boundary your workload crosses: the 512K context cliff, the batch availability gap, or the peak window.</p>
    <p>Answer those three and the per-token price becomes almost irrelevant. Ignore them and the cheapest-looking model on this page is frequently the most expensive one to operate.</p>
  </div>

  {pricing.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="text-gray-500">No pricing records published yet. Phase 2 adds the first verified providers.</p>
  ) : (
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="data-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Chinese AI API pricing comparison</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Provider</th>
            <th>Model</th>
            <th>Input $/1M</th>
            <th>Output $/1M</th>
            <th>Cached input $/1M</th>
            <th>Batch $/1M</th>
            <th>Effective</th>
            <th>Note</th>
            <th>Verified</th>
            <th>Source</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {pricing.flatMap((p) =>
            p.data.models.map((m) => (
              <tr>
                <td><a href={`/pricing/${p.id}/`} class="font-medium">{p.data.provider_id}</a></td>
                <td>{m.model}</td>
                <td>{m.input_price_per_1m ?? '—'}</td>
                <td>{m.output_price_per_1m ?? '—'}</td>
                <td>{m.cached_input_price_per_1m ?? '—'}</td>
                <td>{m.batch_price_per_1m ?? '—'}</td>
                <td>{m.effective_date ?? '—'}</td>
                <td class="note-cell">{m.notes.length > 0 ? (
                  <ul class="note-bullets">
                    {m.notes.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}
                  </ul>
                ) : '—'}</td>
                <td>{p.data.last_verified}</td>
                <td>{m.official_source ? <a href={m.official_source} rel="noopener" target="_blank">link</a> : '—'}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          )}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  )}

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-3">Price structure by provider</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 max-w-3xl">
    Derived from the same records as the table above: how wide each provider's tier ladder is, how much output costs relative to input, and how deep the best cache discount goes.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap mb-6">
    <table class="data-table">
      <caption class="sr-only">Price structure metrics by provider</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Provider</th>
          <th scope="col">Models</th>
          <th scope="col">Currency</th>
          <th scope="col">Input range /1M</th>
          <th scope="col">Tier spread</th>
          <th scope="col">Avg output/input</th>
          <th scope="col">Best cache hit</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {structure.map((s) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={`/pricing/${s.id}/`} class="font-medium">{s.id}</a></td>
            <td>{s.models}</td>
            <td>{s.currency}</td>
            <td>{s.minInput} – {s.maxInput}</td>
            <td>{s.spread.toFixed(1)}x</td>
            <td>{s.ratio ? s.ratio.toFixed(2) : '—'}</td>
            <td>{s.cache != null ? `${s.cache.toFixed(1)}% of input` : '—'}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-4">
    All prices in {new Set(pricing.map((p) => p.data.currency)).size === 1 ? pricing[0]?.data.currency : 'original currency'} per 1M tokens unless noted.
    Always verify against the official pricing page before procurement decisions.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
